<Page title="Accessibility statement" heading="Accessibility" updated="6 November 2026"
  description="How accessible Folio's website, web app and iPhone app are, how we test them against WCAG 2.2 AA, what's known not to work yet, and how to tell us."
  lede="Folio should work for everyone who wants to keep a diary. Here is what we aim for, how we check it, and what still needs work.">
  <h2>What we aim for</h2>
  <p>The website and web app aim to meet the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/" rel="noopener">Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2</a> at level AA. The iPhone app follows Apple’s accessibility guidelines: VoiceOver, Voice Control, Full Keyboard Access, Dynamic Type up to the largest accessibility sizes, Reduce Motion, Reduce Transparency, Increase Contrast and Bold Text.</p>

  <h2>What you can expect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Everything works with a keyboard alone, with a visible focus ring. The web app has shortcuts — press <kbd>?</kbd> to see them.</li>
    <li>Every image that carries meaning has a text alternative; every button has a name, including icon-only ones.</li>
    <li>Text and controls meet AA colour contrast in light and dark mode; colour is never the only signal (task marks, moods and categories also have shapes, words or labels).</li>
    <li>Animation respects your “reduce motion” setting: movement becomes a short fade, and the 3D scenes and seasonal layer stay still.</li>
    <li>Forms have labels; errors are announced and say how to fix them.</li>
    <li>Pages still work when zoomed to 400% or with text spacing increased.</li>
    <li>On iPhone, calendar days read out in full (for example “Tuesday 14 October, 2 entries, 1 task done”), with a rotor for days with entries.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we test</h2>
  <p>Every release is checked with automated tests (axe-core on every website and web-app page, Xcode’s accessibility audit on the main iPhone screens), with keyboard-only and screen-reader passes, and with contrast measured from our colour tokens at build time. The latest results are published with each release in our <a href={site.githubUrl} rel="noopener">source repository</a> (<code>docs/ACCESSIBILITY.md</code>).</p>

  <h2>Known limitations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Dictation and the ✦ writing tools are on iPhone only.</li>
    <li>The web app’s editor follows the iPhone’s formatting rules; some screen readers announce formatting changes inconsistently in rich-text editors.</li>
    <li>Photos you add have no description unless the entry’s words describe them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tell us</h2>
  <p>If something in Folio is hard or impossible for you to use, email <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>. Tell us what you were trying to do and what you use (for example VoiceOver on iPhone, or NVDA with Firefox). We aim to reply within five working days.</p>
</Page>
